{
  "name": "families",
  "character": "Instrument families: what a family of instruments does that another does not. A preset declares `family`; the engine reads the behaviour here, never the instrument's name. A preset that names no family keeps the behaviour it had before families existed.",
  "provenance": "Every number is a starting value until measured on an audited bank (soundbank_audit.py) or a research note. Sources behind the shapes: brass spectral enrichment with dynamic level (Campbell; Stevenson and Campbell, nonlinear propagation, https://www.ioa.org.uk/system/files/proceedings/s_stevenson_dm_campbell_effects_of_non-linear_propagation_on_timbre_of_brass_instruments.pdf, search-result text only); string vibrato delayed after the note onset (Sample Modeling strings review, https://www.soundonsound.com/reviews/audio-modeling-swam-string-sections, search-result text only); typical string vibrato about 6 Hz and about 30 cents (starting value). velocity_brightness (the cutoff is the h-th harmonic of the note's fundamental, h rising with velocity, plus a velocity-driven saturator) and velocity_attack (a soft note rises slower): shapes from the rising high-frequency share with playing level in brass (Gilbert and Myers; Campbell, Institute of Acoustics) and the 50-90 ms acceptable transients of Knutsa's onset-transient times, search-result text only; every number is a starting value tuned on realism_report velocity_response, see knowledgebase/sound-design/sample-realism-equations.md.",
